        "description": "Creates each playlist of a plan from tool:plan-sorting-youtube-watch-later-into-playlists as a public playlist on the same channel, with its description, and adds its videos in batches. It never removes a video and never changes Watch Later. A playlist already on the channel with the same title is reused, never duplicated. What was made is kept in applied_file and each playlist is read back before adding, so running it again adds only what is missing; a recorded playlist that reads back empty stops the run, so a lost sign-in cannot add videos twice. Then verify_sort.py checks each playlist holds the planned number of videos and anyone can see it, that each Watch Later is unchanged, and writes verification.json, INDEX.md and a table of every Watch Later video with its playlists.",
